    "text": "A moving coil galvanometer, having a resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>G</mi></math>&nbsp;produces full scales deflection when a current <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;flows through it. It can be converted into&nbsp;an ammeter of range <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;by connecting a shunt of resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;to it. If it can also be converted into a voltmeter of range <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>G</mi></math>&nbsp;by connecting a resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></msub></math> to it in series, then which among the following is correct?",
